</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"/><td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(1)</span></td><td style="font-size: 10pt; padding-right: 20.05pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Mr.
                                            Travers&#8217;s contract provides for an annual salary of $575,000 beginning on January 1,
                                            2021. As part of our one year salary deferral program that began in May 2024, Mr. Travers
                                            reduced his cash salary by $287,500 in exchange for stock options with a fair market value
                                            of $575,000. The reduction in cash salary was in effect from May 1, 2024 to April 30, 2025.</span></td></tr></table><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"/><td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(2)</span></td><td style="font-size: 10pt; padding-right: 22.4pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Mr.
                                            Russell&#8217;s contract provides for an annual salary of $465,750 beginning on July 1, 2023,
                                            and it had previously been $450,000 since January 1, 2021. As part of our one year salary
                                            deferral program that began in May 2024, Mr. Russell reduced his cash salary by $139,725
                                            in exchange for stock options with a fair market value of $279,450. The reduction in cash
                                            salary was in effect from May 1, 2024 to April 30, 2025.</span></td></tr></table><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"/><td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(3)</span></td><td style="font-size: 10pt; padding-right: 30.6pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Mr.
                                            Jameson's base salary was $439,871 beginning on July 1, 2023, and it had previously been
                                            $425,000 since January 1, 2022. As part of our one year salary deferral program that began
                                            in May 2024, Mr. Jameson reduced his cash salary by $162,752 in exchange for stock options
                                            with a fair market value of $325,505. The reduction in cash salary was in effect from May
                                            1, 2024 to April 30, 2025. Mr. Jameson resigned as chief operating officer on March 11, 2025.</span></td></tr></table><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"/><td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(4)</span></td><td style="font-size: 10pt; padding-right: 30.6pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Mr.
                                            Parkinson's base salary was $360,000 beginning on September 3, 2025 upon joining the Company</span></td></tr></table><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"/><td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(5)</span></td><td style="font-size: 10pt; padding-right: 24.9pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Messrs.
                                            Travers, Russell, and Jameson received cash performance bonuses of $28,750, $18,630, and
                                            $21,994, respectively, in 2025 for meeting certain target elements under the management incentive
                                            bonus program for 2024.</span></td></tr></table><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 24.9pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-left: 0.5in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Messrs.
</span><span style="font-size: 10pt">Travers, Russell, and Jameson received cash performance bonuses of $21,563, $13,736, and $16,216,
respectively, in 2024 for meeting certain target elements under the management incentive bonus program for 2023.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"/><td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(6)</span></td><td style="font-size: 10pt; padding-right: 17.05pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Messrs.
                                            Travers, Russell, and Jameson received 580,808, 282,273, and 328,792, respectively, in stock
                                            options in lieu of cash salary for their participation in the Company&#8217;s salary deferral
                                            program that took effect in May of 2024 and was effective for one year. The fair market value
                                            of the stock options issued was $575,000, $279,450, and $325,505, respectively.</span></td></tr></table><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-left: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Messers.
Travers, Russell, and Jameson received equity performance bonuses of 43,561, 27,751, and 32,761, respectively, in stock options for meeting
certain target elements under the management incentive bonus program for 2023. The fair market value of the stock options issued was
$43,125, $27,473, and $32,433, respectively.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 17.05pt 0pt 30.55pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"/><td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(7)</span></td><td style="font-size: 10pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Mr.
                                            Travers received 145,939 RSUs and 145,939 PSUs as a replacement for the 3,010,000 stock options
                                            that were surrendered under the cancelation of the Company&#8217;s former LTIP effective
                                            in June 2025. The fair market value per share on the date of award of the RSUs and PSUs was
                                            $3.15, resulting in an aggregate fair value of $919,416. </span></td></tr></table><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 30.55pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 30.5pt"></p><div>

