</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 30.5pt"></p><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 30.55pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-left: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Mr. Russell received 59,105
RSUs and 59,105 PSUs as a replacement for the 1,625,000 stock options that were surrendered under the cancelation of the Company&#8217;s
former LTIP effective in June 2025. The fair market value per share on the date of award of the RSUs and PSUs was $3.15, resulting in
an aggregate fair value of $372,362.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 30.55pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-left: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Mr. Parkinson received 150,000
RSUs and 1,000,000 PSUs upon joining the Company as President of its Enterprise Solutions business unit. The fair market value per share
on the date of award of the RSUs and PSUs was $2.15, resulting in an aggregate fair value of $2,472,500.</span></p><div>



</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 30.5pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"/><td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(8)</span></td><td style="font-size: 10pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">The
                                            amounts shown represent the aggregate grant date fair value of stock and option awards computed
                                            in accordance with FASB ASC Topic 718. For information regarding assumptions used in calculating
                                            these amounts, refer to Note 12 to our consolidated financial statements included in our
                                            Annual Report on Form 10-K for the fiscal year ended December 31, 2025.</span></td></tr></table><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 30.55pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"/><td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(9)</span></td><td style="font-size: 10pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Consists
                                            of amounts paid to Mr. Travers as a car allowance (as per his employment contract) and for
                                            health and group life insurance.</span></td></tr></table><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"/><td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(10)</span></td><td style="font-size: 10pt; padding-right: 37.3pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Consists
                                            of amounts paid to Mr. Russell in reimbursement for the rental of an automobile in Rochester,
                                            New York, and direct travel to and from his primary residence in Vancouver, Canada to Rochester,
                                            New York, and for health and group life insurance.</span></td></tr></table><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"/><td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(11)</span></td><td style="font-size: 10pt; padding-right: 37.3pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Consists
                                            of amounts paid to Mr. Jameson for health and group life insurance.</span></td></tr></table><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"/><td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(12)</span></td><td style="font-size: 10pt"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Consists
                                            of amounts paid to Mr. Parkinson for health and group life insurance.</span></td></tr></table><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><span style="font-size: 10pt"><b>&#160;</b></span></p><div>

</div><div><a id="vz_007"></a></div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><span style="font-size: 10pt"><b>PROPOSAL
3</b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><span style="font-size: 10pt"><b>ADVISORY VOTE
ON EXECUTIVE COMPENSATION</b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">The Dodd-Frank Wall
Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (the &#8220;Dodd-Frank Act&#8221;) requires that the Company&#8217;s stockholders have the
opportunity to cast a non-binding advisory vote regarding the approval of the compensation disclosed in this Proxy Statement of the Company&#8217;s
executive officers who are named in the Summary Compensation Table above (&#8220;named executive officers&#8221;). The Company has disclosed
the compensation of the named executive officers pursuant to rules&#160;adopted by the SEC.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">We believe that
our compensation policies for the named executive officers are designed to attract, motivate and retain talented executive officers and
are aligned with the long-term interests of the Company&#8217;s stockholders.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt"><b>Statement on Executive Compensation</b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: left; text-indent: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">To
recruit and retain talent and to reinforce Vuzix&#8217; strategy, our compensation program is designed to be simple, straightforward,
and fair. It is designed as a pay-for-performance compensation program that ensures alignment with Vuzix&#8217; product and technology
growth strategy and shareholder value creation. An important element of the program is our equity award program, which we use to motivate
long-term performance and strongly align the interests of our executives with those of our shareholders. We strive to create an appropriate
balance between our employee retention objectives and our pay-for-performance objectives.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: left; text-indent: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">We
use the following compensation elements to provide an overall competitive compensation and benefits package that is tied to creating
shareholder value and supporting the execution of our short- and long-term business performance and strategies:</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.75in"/><td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><span style=" font-size: 10pt">&#9679;</span></td><td style="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Base
                                            salary;</span></td></tr></table><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.75in"/><td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><span style=" font-size: 10pt">&#9679;</span></td><td style="font-size: 10pt; text-align: left"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Annual
                                            performance bonus incentive plan that focuses on objective key financial drivers with upside
                                            leverage and strategic drivers of the Company&#8217;s long-term success such as the development
                                            of new products and/or technologies (cash and/or restricted stock or short-term equity awards);
                                            and</span></td></tr></table><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.75in"/><td style="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><span style=" font-size: 10pt">&#9679;</span></td><td style="font-size: 10pt; text-align: left"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Long-Term
                                            Incentive Plan (LTIP) incentives tied to internal financial metrics, consisting of restricted
                                            stock awards (RSUs) and performance stock awards (PSUs).</span></td></tr></table><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Our LTIP consists
of a laddered grant program, where the executives receive annual grants of equity that have a 3-year vesting period for the RSUs and
PSUs with a 3-year performance window to vest. The annual split is 50% RSUs and 50% PSUs and results in overlapping multi-year performance
and vesting cycles and the number of these equity units being determined based as a percentage of the executives&#8217; base salary.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"></p><div>

</div><!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 24; Value: 1 --><div>
    </div><div style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1pt solid"><p style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->23<!-- Field: /Sequence --></p></div><div>
    </div><div style="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><p style="margin: 0pt">&#160;</p></div><div>
    </div><!-- Field: /Page --><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"></p><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.5in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
RSUs provide stable, time-based retention value and the PSUs vesting depends on meeting financial targets within a three-year period
and include maximum payouts of 150% of the PSUs based on upside outsized </span><span style="font-size: 10pt">performance. We feel this is the most effective mechanism to align executive interests with long-term shareholder value creation.</span></p><div>



</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: left; text-indent: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">The
combination and allocation of the components, and the target amount of each component, are influenced by the role of the executive officer,
individual performance, expected contributions, market practices, and the total value of all compensation and benefits available to the
individual executive officers. A significant portion of our NEOs&#8217; compensation and awards are at risk, meaning that unless we achieve
certain levels of financial and operational performance, our executives could receive no bonus incentive payouts.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: left; text-indent: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">The
key financial drivers used for both the annual performance bonus and long-term equity compensation elements include revenues, adjusted
EBITDA levels [excludes non-cash items such as depreciation, equity compensation charges, amortization, among other items, and is exclusive
of any bonus payouts under this plan], product margins, and objective strategic measures focused on driving the Company&#8217;s long-term
growth. Each NEO has an established target as a percentage of salary, with a threshold-to-maximum payout equal to +/-33% of target based
on performance relative to target. For the financial goals, results are linearly interpolated between threshold and maximum. A maximum
opportunity of 150% of target can be achieved only by significantly exceeding targeted performance.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">The
Compensation Committee regularly reviews peer equivalent and comparable market practices in executive compensation and governance on
an ongoing basis with the assistance of compensation consultants.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">This advisory stockholder
vote, commonly referred to as a &#8220;say-on-pay vote,&#8221; gives you as a stockholder the opportunity to approve or not approve the
compensation of the named executive officers that is disclosed in this Proxy Statement by voting for or against the following resolution
(or by abstaining with respect to the resolution):</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">RESOLVED, that the stockholders of Vuzix
Corporation approve all of the compensation of the Company&#8217;s executive officers who are named in the Summary Compensation Table
of the Company&#8217;s 2026 Proxy Statement, as such compensation is disclosed in the Company&#8217;s 2026 Proxy Statement pursuant to
Item 402 of Regulation S-K, which disclosure includes the Proxy Statement&#8217;s Summary Compensation Table and other executive compensation
tables and related narrative disclosures.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">In accordance with
the preference expressed by our shareholders at our 2025 Annual Meeting of Stockholders, our Board of Directors determined that the Company
will hold an advisory vote on the compensation of our named executive officers&#160;every year. We expect that the next advisory vote
on the frequency of stockholder votes on executive compensation will occur at our&#160;2031 Annual Meeting of Stockholders.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Although the vote
is non-binding, our Board and the Compensation Committee will review the voting results. To the extent there is a significant negative
vote, we would communicate directly with stockholders to better understand the concerns that influenced the vote. The Board and the Compensation
Committee would consider constructive feedback obtained through this process in making future decisions about executive compensation
programs. However, your non-binding advisory votes described in this Proposal 3 will not be construed: (1)&#160;as overruling any decision
by the Board of Directors, any Board committee or the Company relating to the compensation of the named executive officers, or (2)&#160;as
creating or changing any fiduciary duties or other duties on the part of the Board of Directors, any Board committee or the Company.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"></p><div>

</div><!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 25; Value: 1 --><div>
    </div><div style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1pt solid"><p style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->24<!-- Field: /Sequence --></p></div><div>
    </div><div style="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><p style="margin: 0pt">&#160;</p></div><div>
    </div><!-- Field: /Page --><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><span style="font-size: 10pt"><b>&#160;</b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><span style="font-size: 10pt"><b>RECOMMENDATION
OF THE BOARD FOR PROPOSAL NO. 3:</b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><span style="font-size: 10pt; text-transform: uppercase"><b>Our
Board of Directors recommendS the stockholders vote FOR approval of<br/>
the compensation disclosed in this Proxy Statement of the Company&#8217;s NAMED<br/>
executive officers</b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><span style="font-size: 10pt"><b>OUTSTANDING EQUITY
AWARDS AT FISCAL YEAR END</b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.5in"><span style="font-size: 10pt">The following table
sets forth information concerning exercisable and un-exercisable stock options held by the named executive officers at December&#160;31,
2025.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

